    "description": "The OpenStreetMap Address Auto Complete for Zoho CRM extension helps users quickly search and populate addresses inside Zoho CRM using OpenStreetMap (Nominatim).",
    "longDescription": "<p>Unlike traditional address lookup solutions that rely on paid APIs, this extension uses publicly available OpenStreetMap data, meaning:</p><ul><li>No API keys required</li><li>No usage costs</li><li>Faster deployment</li><li>Clean and modern interface</li><li>Easy address selection</li></ul><p>Users simply click the <strong>Address Search</strong> button, search for a location, and the extension automatically fills the CRM address fields.</p><p><br></p><h1>3. Prerequisites</h1><p>Before installing the extension, ensure:</p><ul><li>Zoho CRM account</li><li>Administrator privileges</li><li>Marketplace installation permissions</li></ul><p>No external services or API subscriptions are required.</p><p><br></p><h1>4. Installation</h1><ol><li>Log in to Zoho CRM.</li><li>Navigate to:</li></ol><p><strong>Setup → Marketplace → All</strong></p><ol><li>Search for:</li></ol><p><strong>OpenStreetMap Address Auto Complete for Zoho CRM</strong></p><ol><li>Click <strong>Install</strong>.</li><li>Choose:</li></ol><ul><li>Install for Admins Only</li><li>Install for All Users</li><li>Select Profiles</li></ul><ol><li>Accept the required permissions.</li><li>Click <strong>Install</strong>.</li></ol><h1>5. Granting Permissions</h1><p>During installation, Zoho CRM will request authorization.</p><p>Click:</p><p><strong>Authorize</strong></p><p>The extension requires permission to:</p><ul><li>Read CRM records</li><li>Update CRM records</li><li>Access CRM metadata</li><li>Open widgets inside CRM</li></ul><p>No external API credentials are requested.</p><p><br></p><h1>6. Initial Setup</h1><p>Once installed:</p><p>Navigate to:</p><p><strong>Setup → Marketplace → Installed Extensions</strong></p><p>Open:</p><p><strong>OpenStreetMap Address Auto Complete</strong></p><p>The extension is immediately ready to use.</p><p>No additional configuration is required.</p><p><br></p><h1>7. Configuring Address Fields</h1><p>The administrator must map the CRM address fields that will receive the selected address data.</p><p>Typical mappings include:</p><p>CRM FieldAddress ValueStreetStreet AddressCityCityStateState / ProvinceZip CodePostal CodeCountryCountry</p><p>Once saved, the configuration applies to all users with access to the extension.</p><p><br></p><h1>8. Using the Extension</h1><h2>Step 1</h2><p>Open any supported CRM record.</p><p>Example:</p><ul><li>Lead</li><li>Contact</li><li>Account</li><li>Vendor</li><li>Custom Module</li></ul><h2>Step 2</h2><p>Locate the button:</p><p><strong>Address Search</strong></p><p>Click the button.</p><p><br></p><h2>Step 3</h2><p>A search window opens.</p><p>Begin typing an address.</p><p>Example:</p><pre class=\"ql-syntax\" spellcheck=\"false\">221B Baker Street London\r\n\r\n</pre><p>Search results appear instantly.</p><p><br></p><h2>Step 4</h2><p>Select the desired address.</p><p>The extension retrieves the address details from OpenStreetMap.</p><p><br></p><h2>Step 5</h2><p>Click:</p><p><strong>Use Address</strong></p><p>The extension automatically populates the configured CRM fields.</p><p>Step 6</p><p>Save the CRM record.</p><p><br></p><h1>9. Supported Modules</h1><p>The extension supports any module containing address fields, including:</p><ul><li>Leads</li><li>Contacts</li><li>Accounts</li><li>Vendors</li><li>Custom Modules</li></ul><p>(Availability depends on your CRM layout and configuration.)</p><p><br></p><h1>10. Best Practices</h1><h3>Verify Search Results</h3><p>Although OpenStreetMap provides reliable address data, always confirm the selected address before saving.</p><h3>Use Standard Address Fields</h3><p>Mapping to Zoho CRM's standard address fields provides the best user experience.</p><h3>Avoid Manual Typing</h3><p>Encourage users to use the search feature instead of entering addresses manually to improve data consistency.</p><h3>Keep Layouts Consistent</h3><p>Use the same address field mappings across modules whenever possible.</p><p><br></p><h1>11. Troubleshooting</h1><h2>No Search Results</h2><p>Possible causes:</p><ul><li>Incorrect spelling</li><li>Incomplete address</li><li>Temporary internet connectivity issue</li></ul><p>Try entering more specific address information.</p><p><br></p><h2>Address Fields Not Populating</h2><p>Verify:</p><ul><li>Field mappings are configured correctly.</li><li>The user has permission to edit the address fields.</li><li>The selected record is in a supported module.</li></ul><h2>Button Not Visible</h2><p>Check:</p><ul><li>Extension installation status.</li><li>User profile permissions.</li><li>CRM layout configuration.</li></ul><h2>Slow Search Response</h2><p>OpenStreetMap relies on internet connectivity. Temporary network latency may affect response times.</p>",
